        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <h3>Why can't I paste an image into Claude Code with Cmd+V?</h3>
        <p>On a Mac, most terminals treat <strong>Cmd+V</strong> as a text paste, which cannot carry image data. Claude Code listens for <strong>Ctrl+V</strong> instead (Cmd+V works in iTerm2). On Windows and WSL the key is <strong>Alt+V</strong>.</p>

        <h3>What is the shortcut to paste an image in Claude Code on Windows?</h3>
        <p><strong>Alt+V</strong> on Windows and WSL. Under WSL both Ctrl+V and Alt+V are bound, and the documentation suggests Alt+V if your terminal intercepts Ctrl+V.</p>

        <h3>How do I add an image if paste does not work at all?</h3>
        <p>Drag the image file into the window, or type its path in your prompt, for example <code>Analyze this image: /path/to/your/image.png</code>. Neither method uses the clipboard.</p>

        <h3>Why does image paste fail over SSH?</h3>
        <p>The tool reads the clipboard of the machine it runs on. Over SSH that is the remote server, which never received your screenshot. Save the image locally, copy it to the server, and give the tool the file path.</p>

